<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Hasani</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">10th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Hasani was a descendant of the Prophet's grandson al-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hasan-ibn-ali">Hasan ibn Ali</a> who took control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a> in the 960s, around the time the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimids</a> conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>. He founded the line of Hasanid sharifs who governed the holy city, usually acknowledging whichever Muslim power ruled Egypt, and so began the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sharif-of-mecca">Sharifate of Mecca</a> that lasted until 1925.</p></div>
